SO-ARM101 arm chain
===================

Vendored source
---------------
    Upstream design: TheRobotStudio / SO-ARM100 (SO-ARM101 revision)
    https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100
    Licence: Apache-2.0

    Local calibrated description: jdamr_cube_description (JD-AMR Cube 실기)
    Joint origins, axes and limits are taken from the chain that has been
    verified on physical hardware in this lab. The kinematics reference is
    capstone_pick/kinematics.py in the same workspace.

Copied scope
------------
    so101_arm.urdf.xacro   generated by scripts/generate_so101_arm_xacro.py
                           from the calibrated JD-AMR description
    ../../meshes/so101/    12 STL meshes of the SO-ARM101 arm

Not included
------------
    The upstream single rotating jaw is not used. This project uses the
    ggao50 SO101 Parallel Gripper instead. Because that repository carries
    no licence statement, its meshes are NOT redistributed here. The URDF
    uses a dimensional proxy authored for this project in
    urdf/ggao50_gripper.xacro, based on measurements of the published STLs.

        https://github.com/ggao50/SO101-Parallel-Gripper

Joint convention
----------------
    shoulder_pan   limit  +/- 1.91986 rad
    shoulder_lift  limit  +/- 1.74533 rad
    elbow_flex     limit  +/- 1.69000 rad
    wrist_flex     limit  +/- 1.65806 rad
    wrist_roll     limit  -2.74385 .. 2.84121 rad

    Names match arm_shoulder_pan / arm_shoulder_lift / arm_elbow_flex /
    arm_wrist_flex / arm_wrist_roll in the JD-AMR chain, with the arm_
    prefix replaced by the left_ / right_ macro prefix.
